Below is a **clean, exhaustive, implementation-ready delta list** you should follow.
This is **ONLY differences vs IVPLT** — nothing repeated.

---

## 1️⃣ Fundamental Nature

**IVPLT**

* Vertical **compression**
* Measures **settlement (downward)**

**RVPLT**

* Vertical **compression**
* Measures **settlement (downward)**

**Lateral**

* **Horizontal** load
* Measures **lateral deflection**

**Uplift / Pull-out**

* Vertical **tension**
* Measures **upward movement**

---

## 2️⃣ Governing IS Code Clauses

* **IVPLT** → IS 2911 Part 4, Clause **7.1.5**
* **RVPLT** → IS 2911 Part 4, Clause **7.1.5.1**
* **Lateral** → IS 2911 Part 4, Clause **8.4 / 8.4.1**
* **Uplift** → IS 2911 Part 4, Clause **9.4**

---

## 3️⃣ Test Load Multiplier (CRITICAL)

| Test Type             | Test Load vs Design                       |
| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| **IVPLT**             | **2.5 ×** design load                     |
| **RVPLT**             | **1.5 ×** design load                     |
| **Lateral – Initial** | **2.5 ×** design lateral load             |
| **Lateral – Routine** | **1.0 ×** design lateral load *(default)* |
| **Uplift**            | **2.5 ×** design uplift load              |

---

## 4️⃣ Acceptance / Failure Criterion

### IVPLT

Safe load = **LESSER of**

* **⅔ × load at 12 mm settlement**
* **½ × load at 10% pile dia settlement**

---

### RVPLT

No “safe load calc”. **PASS / FAIL only**

Settlement at **1.5× load must be ≤**

* **12 mm** → pile dia ≤ 600 mm
* **18 mm OR 2% dia (whichever less)** → dia > 600 mm

---

### Lateral

Safe lateral load = **LEAST of**

* Load at **5 mm lateral deflection**
* **½ × load at 12 mm deflection** *(if reached)*

Most reports only use **5 mm rule**

---

### Uplift

Safe uplift load = **LEAST of**

* **⅔ × load at 12 mm uplift**
* **½ × load at yield / break point** *(manual if visible)*

---

## 5️⃣ Direction of Dial Gauge Reading

| Test    | Movement   |
| ------- | ---------- |
| IVPLT   | Downward   |
| RVPLT   | Downward   |
| Lateral | Horizontal |
| Uplift  | Upward     |

---

## 6️⃣ Reaction System

| Test    | Reaction                                    |
| ------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| IVPLT   | Kentledge / Anchor piles                    |
| RVPLT   | Kentledge / Anchor piles                    |
| Lateral | **Reaction pile / frame (horizontal jack)** |
| Uplift  | **Anchor pile + tension jack**              |

---

## 7️⃣ Dial Gauge Configuration

| Test    | Gauges                                  |
| ------- | --------------------------------------- |
| IVPLT   | 3–4 gauges on pile head                 |
| RVPLT   | 3–4 gauges on pile head                 |
| Lateral | **2 on test pile + 2 on reaction pile** |
| Uplift  | 2–4 gauges measuring uplift             |

⚠️ **Lateral requires NET deflection = test pile − reaction pile**

---

## 8️⃣ Load Holding Logic

| Test    | Holding                                     |
| ------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| IVPLT   | Long holds + **24-hr creep often required** |
| RVPLT   | 30–60 min holds                             |
| Lateral | Hold until **rate < 0.1 mm / 30 min**       |
| Uplift  | Similar to IVPLT but no 24-hr usually       |

